{"t":1793977381740,"p":{"session_id":"c933c676-8109-40dc-9689-b282f3574e3c","transcript_path":"/home/user/.claude/projects/-home-user-proj/c933c676-8109-40dc-9689-b282f3574e3c.jsonl","cwd":"/home/user/proj","prompt_id":"db2cb465-67cc-4023-aa15-b0451f49cd19","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"UserPromptSubmit","prompt":"Do these steps in order, using the tools named:\n1. Use TaskCreate to create four tasks: \"scaffold\", \"fix tests\", \"survey\", \"summarize\".\n2. Mark \"scaffold\" in_progress. Use Write to create calc.py with a function add(a, b) that returns a - b (a deliberate bug), and test_calc.py that imports add, asserts add(2, 3) == 5, then prints \"ok\". Mark \"scaffold\" completed.\n3. Mark \"fix tests\" in_progress. Run `python3 test_calc.py` with Bash. It will fail. Run that exact same command two more times, one call at a time and without changing any file, to rule out a flaky test. Then fix calc.py with Edit and run `python3 test_calc.py` again until it prints ok. Mark \"fix tests\" completed.\n4. Mark \"survey\" in_progress. In one message, launch two Explore subagents in parallel with the Agent tool: one reads calc.py and describes it in one sentence, the other reads test_calc.py and describes it in one sentence. Wait for both reports. Mark \"survey\" completed.\n5. Mark \"summarize\" in_progress, reply with a two-line summary, then mark \"summarize\" completed."}}
